<title>GERMANY: Portugal &quot;good bet&quot; for EMU -- Spain's Rato.</title>
<headline>Portugal &quot;good bet&quot; for EMU -- Spain's Rato.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal is a &quot;good bet&quot; to qualify for the first wave of European Monetary Union (EMU) in 1999, Spain's Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Rato told the Federation of German Chambers of Commerce that decisions on who would qualify for the start of monetary union must be based purely on economic data.</p>
<p>&quot;Portugal is a good bet, if you want to know my opinion,&quot; Rato said. &quot;Portugal has made very good efforts in the past few years...I think Portugal is on its own merits a good candidate for monetary union.&quot;</p>
<p>Rato was in Bonn ahead of bilateral cabinet consultations on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Kevin Liffey, Bonn newsroom +49-228-26097160</p>
</text>
